    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual's example supports geographical-origin description as a possible basis for a finding of no inherent adaptation, here together with a quality reference. This is an inferred relationship concerning descriptive references, not a claim that geographical origin itself invariably produces that finding."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.4e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the example's combined origin-and-quality reasoning supports a separate relationship for geographical origin."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0128" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:aeeec17d7c222fefa6c1732a21693a2733ee591be2d3fefe65bacce528df82fb" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 972 ;
    tmk:spanStart 718 ;
    tmk:supportingText "As merely a reference to origin and quality, the trade mark as a whole has no inherent adaptation to distinguish and will attract grounds for rejection under section 41(6) or 41(3) for trade mark applications with a filing date on or after 15 April 2013." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0130 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0004 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0019 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly identifies geographical origin as a subject about which confusion could arise. Mapping that statement to this predicate is inferred: the potential source is a connotation concerning geographical origin, not the geographical origin itself."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the ontology should instead represent geographical origin as the subject of confusion, rather than its potential source."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0130" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:deb607cbc7ae6fd37a648887567b1d4002a2af161e5ab51e486bee19095a59a0" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1277 ;
    tmk:spanStart 891 ;
    tmk:supportingText "For example, deception or confusion could arise in regard to the: Character of the goods and/or services including their composition, nature or other properties Quality or quantity of the goods and/or services Geographical origin of the goods and/or services Intended use or purpose of the goods and/or services Connection in the mind of the buying public with a person or organisation." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0131 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0002 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0022 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects use of a mark identical to or connoting a notified INN with likely deception or confusion where the specification is not restricted to the indicated substance. The relationship is inferred at the concept level: an INN alone does not produce that likelihood."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether mayGiveRiseTo adequately preserves the conditions concerning the mark and specification."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0131" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:86800dcce4d41f73e2792ad626162693402011f3c8ba4135bbf91f045f2a7b2f" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/4> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 434 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A ground for rejection under section 43 exists where a trade mark, or part of a trade mark, to be used in relation to pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances is the same as, or may connote, a notified INN and use of the trade mark in respect of the goods covered by the specification are not restricted to the particular substance indicated by the INN. Use of such a trade mark would be likely to give rise to deception or confusion." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

