    tmk:supportingText "A ground for rejection under section 43 exists where a trade mark, or part of a trade mark, to be used in relation to pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances is the same as, or may connote, a notified INN and use of the trade mark in respect of the goods covered by the specification are not restricted to the particular substance indicated by the INN. Use of such a trade mark would be likely to give rise to deception or confusion." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0135 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0024 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0038 ;
