    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A mark lacking inherent adaptation may be shown through evidence of use to be capable of distinguishing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the sentence states this relationship, read the way the predicate reads."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0206" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:aad70a11e0e6736dd677702d9ee88e4aaf15d7d35f711f9eafbc58473d49c47f" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 430 ;
    tmk:spanStart 221 ;
    tmk:supportingText "This situation is most likely to occur when a trade mark which is lacking in inherent adaptation to distinguish is shown through evidence of use to be capable of distinguishing when used in particular colours." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0208 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0060 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0059 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The judicial extract reproduced in the Manual expressly requires consideration of ordinary signification when determining inherent adaptation. The required element is that consideration, not that the mark must possess an ordinary signification."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the relation needs an express scope restriction to trade marks consisting of words."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0208" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:aa6ecd7478725f377ac835ee6aa871aa254c11c537628f73f33613313b23f1fc" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~5> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 415 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "[70] In accordance with the principles established in Mark Foy’s and restated in Clark Equipment, Faulding and Burger King, determining whether a trade mark is “inherently adapted to distinguish”, as required by s 41(3), requires consideration of the “ordinary signification” of the words proposed as trade marks to any person in Australia concerned with the goods to which the proposed trade mark is to be applied." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0209 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0061 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0059 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly identifies assessment of other traders' legitimate desire to use as the second part of determining inherent adaptation. This requires assessing the likelihood of that desire, not establishing that the desire exists."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the descriptive wording of the two-part process warrants must modality."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0209" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:5a98371ccfdfb4a4f333e505716c18c9c7b6fb903adb5be22c344fb6a950ad3e" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 602 ;
    tmk:spanStart 244 ;
    tmk:supportingText "This determination involves a two-part process: firstly, determining the ordinary signification of the trade mark in the light of the applied for goods and/or services; and secondly, determining the likelihood that other traders might legitimately wish to use the trade mark for that ordinary signification in connection with their similar goods or services." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0210 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0119 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0060 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual uses the device’s ordinary signification to explain why it would not be prima facie capable of distinguishing for the depicted goods. This supports ordinary signification as a factor qualifying that assessment, rather than as an automatic bar for every sign."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether qualifies adequately captures the role of ordinary signification in assessing prima facie distinguishing capacity."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0210" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:7a94aca19143cea39c149332e0a2740a9c86b85e5571ce007028806f0255ed5d" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/25/25/1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 410 ;
    tmk:spanStart 166 ;
    tmk:supportingText "For example, the ordinary signification of picture of a wheelbarrow is “this is a wheelbarrow”. Hence an imageof a wheelbarrow for wheelbarrows would not be prima facie capable of distinguishing any one trader's wheelbarrows in the marketplace." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

