    tmk:spanEnd 637 ;
    tmk:spanStart 439 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If, having regard to the evidence and the circumstances, an examiner is satisfied it is proper for the application to be accepted, then it is appropriate to exercise the discretion under s 44(3)(b)." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0232 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0064 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0071 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual makes the continued presence of closely related goods and services relevant to whether a proposed deletion removes a section 44 conflict. This supports a qualifying relationship, rather than making close relatedness sufficient by itself to establish conflict."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether qualifies adequately captures the role of close relatedness in assessing removal of a section 44 conflict."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0232" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:c269b8fbd6d575292e41f251453b78d35f41eb72315d8c6bd0b68c6db48a3bd6" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/3/3/1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 311 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "An applicant may attempt to overcome grounds for rejection raised under s 44 by deleting goods and/or services so as to remove all conflict with the goods/services of the earlier trade mark(s). The examiner must consider whether a proposed deletion removes all similar and/or closely related goods and services." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0233 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0109 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0071 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states that meeting the close-relatedness tests can strengthen the case for defensive registration. It treats relatedness as a favourable consideration, not a necessary element of defensive registration."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.4e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether qualifies should attach to the case for defensive registration rather than the broader defensive trade mark concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0233" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:a57e4418e59f41b935456ec5cb1c8588fafbc2f3fd34c3142424880aa6aab3dd" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/6/6/2/5> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 445 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "In general, it will be easier for the applicant to make a case for defensive registration if the goods or services specified in the application are in some way related to those in respect of which the trade mark has already been registered and used. This is likely to be the case if the usual tests for “goods of the same description” and “closely related services” and for “services of the same description” and “closely related goods” are met." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0234 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0073 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:broader ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0074 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly treats a non-traditional sign as a kind of sign. The quoted application requirement is separate from this taxonomic relationship."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the neighbour's alternative label 'non-traditional trade mark' needs to be distinguished from the sign itself."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0234" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:kindOfAffirmed "The Manual speaks of \"a sign that is a colour, scent, shape, sound, aspect of packaging or other kind of non-traditional sign\" (Part 10.3). Every non-traditional sign is a sign; the bare word \"sign\" does not name the narrower idea."@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:1d982c58b3d28286c6eb771db338502d84c7eea9bf958b860cd4860f40b70928" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 519 ;
    tmk:spanStart 245 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Additionally, in the case of a trade mark that consists of or contains a sign that is a colour, scent, shape, sound, aspect of packaging or other kind of non-traditional sign, the application must include a concise and accurate description of the trade mark (subreg 4.3(7))." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

