    tmk:spanEnd 191 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "An examiner will need to consider whether the presence of an INN stem in a word is “meaningful” enough to give rise to a connotation leading to likely deception or confusion under section 43." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0384 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0001 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0048 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual permits consideration of whether an existing connotation would be understood as fanciful or unrealistic, qualifying its assessment rather than denying its existence. This passage does not expressly extend that treatment to every ambiguous geographic reference."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the neighbour's inclusion of ambiguous geographic references is supported by this passage."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0384" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "may" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:ee8650d8222dab43788198d8fd9f43ca934317a389f76728bdf40f85c97ac032" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/4%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1558 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1369 ;
    tmk:supportingText "When considering trade marks that include a clear connotation, the concept that this connotation would be understood as a fanciful or unrealistic description can also be taken into account." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0385 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0001 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0030 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual supports the inference that an image of a person may give rise to a connotation, while expressly rejecting mere presence as sufficient for a section 43 ground. The causal relationship is inferred from the conditional examination guidance."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this relationship should be confined to images of well-known persons, given the passage's opening scope."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0385" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:94219eaa9c113dcecb64f0c0d8b7d7970ee0c89b4e732ebf371d1b1b4f2abcf1" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6/6/1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 892 ;
    tmk:spanStart 614 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A section 43 ground for rejection should not be raised merely because a trade mark contains the image of a person. The section 43 ground for rejection should only be raised if the examiner considers that the confusing or deceptive connotation discussed above is likely to arise." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0386 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0002 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0145 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual makes expected geographical origin and the specification’s coverage of goods from elsewhere relevant to assessing deception or confusion. This supports the relationship for geographical origin generally; its extension to the wine-specific legal test is uncertain."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.2e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether GC-0145 encompasses ordinary geographical origin or is confined to the statutory wine-specific meaning."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0386" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:17c928f3bdc152f1ba5a886c36379eb9e74ab1b2afcb0cef15aa9cc5ee4cf3d6" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1564 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1116 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If a trade mark containing a geographical reference is found to connote geographical origin, consideration must then be given to whether ordinary consumers would be deceived or confused as a result. This includes assessing whether the scope of the specification would include goods/services produced in areas outside the geographical location when a consumer would reasonably expect them to originate from the location referenced in the trade mark." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

