    tmk:authoringReasoning "The delegate’s statement quoted in the Manual expressly makes reputation a factor qualifying the assessment of likely confusion. This is a criterion reported by the Manual, not legislative wording, and reputation alone is expressly insufficient in the surrounding passage."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.1e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the anchor’s general reputation concept extends to the opponent’s trade mark reputation discussed here."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0474" ;
