    tmk:spanEnd 624 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The legislation states that \"an application lapses if it is not accepted within the prescribed period or within that period as extended in accordance with the regulations\" (section 37). The prescribed period is 15 months from the date of the first report, or 15 months from the date of any further report that raises new grounds for rejection of the application. This is the basic time period within which an applicant for a trade mark is expected to finalise the application to the point of acceptance. If an applicant requests an ex parte hearing on an exam matter, the Registrar will defer acceptance of that application." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

