    tmk:authoringReasoning "prescribed sign is a sign prescribed for the purposes of section 39(2), as a mark may contain one: something a trade mark contains or conveys — a word, name, image or sign within it, or a meaning — so `sign_content`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0198 may give rise to section 39 ground for rejection; GR-0199 may give rise to section 39 ground for rejection."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "sign_content" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is better read as something about the mark's context than about what the mark itself contains or conveys."@en-AU ;
