tmka:GT-0066 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "honest concurrent use is two traders' honest use of their marks side by side: something a person does with a trade mark in the course of trade — using it, or authorising its use — so `use_in_trade`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0220: conflict with other signs is overcome by it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "use_in_trade" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is use itself, or a circumstance about use that belongs with context."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0066" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/2%231> .

tmka:GT-0067 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "prior use is an applicant's use of its mark before another's: something a person does with a trade mark in the course of trade — using it, or authorising its use — so `use_in_trade`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0219: conflict with other signs is overcome by it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "use_in_trade" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is use itself, or a circumstance about use that belongs with context."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0067" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> .

tmka:GT-0068 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "other circumstances is circumstances, other than concurrent or prior use, that make acceptance proper: something outside the trade mark that the assessment looks at — the goods, the market and its consumers, a person or place, a reputation, a date — so `context`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0229: conflict with other signs is overcome by it; GR-0231 may give rise to acceptance."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "context" ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is something outside the mark at all, or a meaning the mark itself conveys (sign content)."@en-AU ;
