tmka:GT-0079 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A single application covering two or more marks that resemble each other in material particulars. The concept names the set of marks — what is applied for."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'series of trade marks' and 'divisional application' fall on the same side. This pass puts series in subject_matter and divisional in procedural_step, on the reading that a series is a thing applied for and a division is something done to an application. A reviewer who thinks both are applications should move series; one who thinks both are mechanisms should move divisional. They should be decided together."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0079" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51> .

tmka:GT-0080 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A question that has to be answered before a series application is valid."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "legal_test" ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0080" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51> .

tmka:GT-0081 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "use of a trade mark is using a trade mark in the course of trade: something a person does with a trade mark in the course of trade — using it, or authorising its use — so `use_in_trade`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0508 qualifies evidence of use; GR-0520 qualifies defensive trade mark."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "use_in_trade" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is use itself, or a circumstance about use that belongs with context."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0081" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0082 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "authorised use is use of a trade mark by an authorised user under the owner's control: something a person does with a trade mark in the course of trade — using it, or authorising its use — so `use_in_trade`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. No edge yet says what it does to which ground or test — a gap the relate job and the edge audit look for."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "use_in_trade" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is use itself, or a circumstance about use that belongs with context."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0082" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> .

tmka:GT-0083 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 8(1) defines the authorised user as a person — the one who uses the mark under the owner's control. The concept record already separates the person from the use, and it is the person this record types."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "process_role" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'authorised user' the party and 'authorised use' the fact should both be concepts. If they should, typing only the party leaves the more examinable half of the pair unheld by anything."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0083" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> .

tmka:GT-0084 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 defines the registered owner as the person in whose name the mark is registered. A party, identified by an entry rather than constituted by one."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "process_role" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether registered owner and applicant are one party at two stages or two concepts. Part 19B treats the registration as personal property held by that person, and a role typing carries none of that."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0084" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-owner> .

tmka:GT-0085 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "predecessor in title is a person from whom the applicant's title to the mark derives: a person or body that acts — who does something — so `process_role`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0493 qualifies prior use."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "process_role" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this person acts in the process, or is only someone the assessment refers to."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0085" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> .

tmka:GT-0086 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Ownership passes from one party to another by act of the parties. A change of state in an application or a registration."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether assignment and transmission are two concepts or one with two modes. Part 43's title carries both and the section 6 definitions split them, so the corpus supports either reading."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0086" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/assignment> .

tmka:GT-0087 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The other half of the pair: ownership passes without an act of the parties. Still a change of state."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "As at GT-0086. Note also that GC-0087's evidence comes from the Manual rather than from the section 6 definition, because that definition is a stub — so this typing rests on the Manual's gloss."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0087" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/1%231~1> .

tmka:GT-0088 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A trade mark in a particular state — one whose particulars are entered in the Register. A thing, defined by an entry rather than being one."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether registered trade mark is a concept beside GC-0072 or GC-0072 in a state, which would make it narrower rather than a sibling."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0088" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-trade-mark> .

tmka:GT-0089 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The record kept under section 207. The thing entries are made in."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "instrument_or_record" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The concept's record warns that the Register, the old register and the Record of International Registrations must not be merged. This group holds one of the three; the other two are held by nothing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0089" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/register> .

tmka:GT-0091 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "filing date is the date an application is filed: something outside the trade mark that the assessment looks at — the goods, the market and its consumers, a person or place, a reputation, a date — so `context`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0269 qualifies renewal of registration; GR-0524 qualifies evidence of use; GR-0525 qualifies convention application."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "context" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is something outside the mark at all, or a meaning the mark itself conveys (sign content)."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0091" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> .

tmka:GT-0092 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 31 makes examination the act the Registrar must perform, with two subjects and only two. The step that produces an acceptance or a report."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the vocabulary should hold examination the process and the report it produces separately. The Act says 'examine and report on', which is two things, and this concept holds one."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0092" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s31> .

tmka:GT-0093 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The point at which an application changes state. Section 33 makes acceptance the thing that must follow examination unless the Registrar is satisfied of a defect or a ground."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether typing acceptance as a step loses the presumption of registrability. That presumption is the most examinable thing about section 33, no concept in this group carries it, and the reviewer's own note (OQ-0015) said the office's actual bar for it is not in the knowledge base either."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0093" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> .

tmka:GT-0095 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A registration is undone under sections 84A to 84D in circumstances where it appears it should not have occurred. A transition."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The Manual records that the Registrar is not obliged to consider revocation even where a third party requests it. That discretion is a modality on the step, and this group carries no modality — which is a limit of the group rather than of the record."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0095" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part62/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0096 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The acceptance period is, in the Manual's own words, set in abeyance. A change in the state of an application."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Deferment suspends a period and an extension of time lengthens one. Both are typed procedural_step. If that distinction matters to retrieval, the group is too coarse to carry it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0096" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0097 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A period set by the Act or Regulations is lengthened on request. A change in the state of the thing whose period it is."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The Manual notes the procedure differs by which time is being extended — one concept covering many procedures. The group hides that variability rather than expressing it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0097" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/1%231~1> .

tmka:GT-0098 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "An application ends on the expiry of the acceptance period. Typed here on the reading that the group holds transitions and not only acts, which is why the class comment says so in terms."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether an event nobody performs belongs beside acts somebody does. If it does not, the group splits and lapsing needs a home — and GT-0123 (withdrawal) is the record to compare it against, because withdrawal differs from lapsing precisely in that a person does it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0098" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/1/1/1> .

tmka:GT-0099 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A limitation of the exclusive rights given by registration, entered against the mark."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "instrument_or_record" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The Manual's own gloss is that the owner never had exclusive rights in the disclaimed part anyway — so a disclaimer records a position rather than changing one. That is the argument for this group and it is worth testing directly."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0099" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part24/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0103 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A document — and, on the Regulations' definition, two: a notice of intention to oppose plus a statement of grounds and particulars."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "instrument_or_record" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The concept is a composite of two separately defined terms, so the corpus holds three related definitions and the vocabulary holds one. Whether the components should be concepts is a vocabulary question this typing does not reach."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0103" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0104 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A proceeding that removes a mark from the Register for non-use. A transition, grounded by the Manual in section 17's requirement that a mark be used."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The onus sits on the opponent once the removal application is opposed, which is unusual and is a property of the proceeding. Nothing in this group carries an onus."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0104" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0105 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Amendment or cancellation of an entry in the Register, resulting from an order of a prescribed court. A transition."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "This is the only step in the group performed by a court rather than by the Registrar. If the vocabulary needs that visible, it is a property of the step and not a reason for a different group."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0105" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part42/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0106 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A registration is renewed at ten-year intervals. A change of state, and one that recurs."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "procedural_step" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Any person may effect a renewal, not only the owner. The group does not carry who may act, and here that is a substantive fact about the step."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0106" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part40/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0107 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A kind of registration, distinguishing certified goods or services from uncertified ones. What is applied for, under different conditions."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Certification, collective and defensive marks are three registrations with different conditions, and GC-0088 is the ordinary one. Whether the vocabulary wants a 'kinds of registration' level between them and 'trade mark' is a modelling question this typing does not answer."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0107" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part35/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0108 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A kind of registration, distinguishing members' goods or services from non-members'."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Certification, collective and defensive marks are three registrations with different conditions, and GC-0088 is the ordinary one. Whether the vocabulary wants a 'kinds of registration' level between them and 'trade mark' is a modelling question this typing does not answer."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0108" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0109 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A kind of registration, available where an existing registration has a reputation extensive enough that use on other goods would suggest a connection."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The alternative above. If the vocabulary wants 'no intention to use required' as an exception in its own right, this concept keeps its group and the exception is a second record that does not yet exist. Certification, collective and defensive marks are three registrations with different conditions, and GC-0088 is the ordinary one. Whether the vocabulary wants a 'kinds of registration' level between them and 'trade mark' is a modelling question this typing does not answer."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0109" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/1/1/1> .

tmka:GT-0111 tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "convention application is an application claiming priority from an earlier one in a Convention country: a document, entry or endorsement the process produces or receives, or writes to the Register — so `instrument_or_record`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0408 qualifies priority date; GR-0602 qualifies date of registration."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "instrument_or_record" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this is a document or entry in itself, or the step that produces it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0111" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part11/1/1/2> .

tmka:GT-0112 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A treaty, administered by WIPO's International Bureau. Not a rule the Act makes: Australian practice gives effect to it. Keeping that visible is CLAUDE.md rule 5 applied one level up — the Manual is practice and not law, and the Protocol is neither Australian law nor Australian practice."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "external_instrument" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether a two-member group is worth having at all, and if it is, whether the Nice Classification belongs in it beside a treaty. Those are the only two members and they are not obviously the same kind of thing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0112" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> .

tmka:GT-0113 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
