    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "reputation of a trade mark is a trade mark's being known in Australia: something outside the trade mark that the assessment looks at — the goods, the market and its consumers, a person or place, a reputation, a date — so `context`. Retyped on the owner's ruling B1 of 2026-10-09 (ADR-0126): a kind says what a concept is, and what it does is an edge. What it does is on its edges: GR-0084 may give rise to deception; GR-0555 qualifies defensive trade mark."@en-AU ;
