    tmk:authoringReasoning "Typed in the same judgement as the concept: The Regulations expressly define the term, and section 27 supplies the application requirements and required contents. The application is best treated as an instrument or record, rather than the act of filing or the trade mark sought to be registered. No existing concept covers the general application: divisional and convention applications are more specific concepts, while examination, acceptance and amendment concern its processing. The regulatory definition is substantive rather than merely a direction to another definition, so it is retained as the definition quote."@en-AU ;
