    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Typed in the same judgement as the concept: The Regulations expressly define this notice by reference to operative filing provisions. It is a distinct document, not the opposition itself or the notice of opposition already represented in the ontology. The quoted provision supplies the IRDA holder’s filing obligation, address-for-service requirement and provision of a copy to the opponent. Regulation 17A.48Q separately governs a notice filed by the applicant in an opposition concerning cessation of protection. The Manual explains its role in contesting opposition to registration or protection, but that explanation is Registrar practice rather than legislation."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "instrument_or_record" ;
