tmkc:GC-0145 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:Context,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: In relation to wine, this statutory concept ties origin in a country, region or locality to where the grapes used to make the wine were grown."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "originate, in relation to wine"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "originate"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly gives 'originate' a statutory meaning in relation to wine by referring to section 15. Section 15 supplies necessary conditions for attributing geographical origin to wine, supporting a distinct legal-test concept rather than a generic English verb. The Manual passages use 'originate' more generally for commercial source and do not define this wine-specific test. The supplied label for GC-0019 suggests possible overlap, but does not establish that it already holds this specialised test."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check whether GC-0019 geographical origin already encompasses this wine-specific statutory test; only its label has been supplied."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0145" ;
    tmk:labelKey "originate",
        "originate in relation to wine" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6> ;
    tmk:notLabel "business identifier"@en-AU,
        "geographical indication"@en-AU,
        "geographical origin"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "business identifier",
        "geographical indication",
        "geographical origin" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "originate" ;
    tmk:qualifies tmkc:GC-0002 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0145 .

tmkc:GC-0148 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A lawyer is a statutorily defined legal professional whom the Manual identifies as an example of someone an applicant may authorise to make an evidence declaration on their behalf."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "lawyer"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly defines the term, and the Manual passages give lawyers a procedural role as possible authorised declarants. This is a distinct process role, not a generic phrase or an existing concept. The declaration guidance is Registrar practice, whereas the definition is statutory. None of the listed PROVISIONS is supplied with text establishing a legislative basis for this role."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/lawyer> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The supplied passages do not establish how the cited sections 41(3), 41(4) and 44 ground this role; check those links before recording them as legislative bases."@en-AU ;
    tmk:files tmkc:GC-0041 ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0148" ;
    tmk:labelKey "lawyer" ;
    tmk:notLabel "trade mark attorney"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "trade mark attorney" ;
