tmkc:GC-0056 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "A resemblance test that is not the section 44 one. The comparison is between the applicant's sign and a prescribed or prohibited sign, and the threshold is 'likely to be taken for it' rather than 'likely to deceive or cause confusion'."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "so nearly resembling as to be likely to be taken for it"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "so nearly resembling"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The phrase is the Act's and the Manual quotes it as the operative test for subparagraph 39(2)(b)(i). It is held as a separate concept from deceptive similarity because the two use different words for different comparisons, and collapsing them would let a section 44 authority be cited into a section 39 question."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/2%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether practice in fact applies the section 10 case law to this test. If it does, the two concepts are more closely related than this record says."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0056" ;
    tmk:labelKey "so nearly resembling",
        "so nearly resembling as to be likely to be taken for it" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s39(2)(b)> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo tmkc:GC-0063 ;
    tmk:notLabel "deceptively similar"@en-AU,
        "substantially identical"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "deceptively similar",
        "substantially identical" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "so nearly resembling" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s39>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/2%231> ;
    tmk:statesThresholdFor tmkc:GC-0182 ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0056 .

tmkc:GC-0082 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:UseInTrade ;
    rdfs:comment "Control by the owner is the whole of it: section 8(2) makes use authorised only to the extent the user acts under the owner's control. Section 7(3) then treats authorised use as use by the owner, which is why it matters to section 41 and section 44(4)."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "authorised use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:broader tmkc:GC-0081 ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "authorised use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 8 defines it and limits it by control. Held apart from 'authorised user' because the Act defines the person in 8(1) and the use in 8(2), and evidence questions attach to the second."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 19A passage on control rather than the general opening. This record cites the opening because it names authorised use in the list of questions use bears on."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0082" ;
    tmk:isAttributedTo tmkc:GC-0085 ;
    tmk:labelKey "authorised use",
        "authorised use of a trade mark" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8(2)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "assignment"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "assignment",
        "authorised user",
        "use of a trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "authorised use" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0082 .

tmkc:GC-0085 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Load-bearing in two places at once: section 41(5) makes a predecessor's use count as the applicant's for distinctiveness, and section 44(4) does the same for prior use. The section 6 definition itself is a stub that continues into a list."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "predecessor in title"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Act states the consequence in terms in section 41(5); the section 6 definition is a stub whose text does not carry the substance, so the evidence is drawn from the operative provision instead."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the concept should carry the section 6 list as narrower concepts. The stub continues into subparagraphs this record does not reach."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0085" ;
    tmk:labelKey "predecessor in title" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(5)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(4)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/predecessor-in-title> ;
    tmk:notLabel "assignment"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "assignment",
        "authorised user",
        "registered owner" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "predecessor in title" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0085 .

tmkc:GC-0116 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Defined by the Act as the person in whose name the application currently stands — so the applicant can change without the application changing. The Manual's Part 10 treats getting the identity right as a formality requirement in its own right."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "applicant"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms, and the 'for the time being' clause is the part worth keeping — it is what makes assignment of a pending application coherent."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be Part 10.1 on the name requirement or a passage about who may apply under section 27."@en-AU ;
