    tmk:authoringReasoning "The term names an expressly defined statutory class of courts, not a generic phrase or an existing concept. Section 6 refers to section 190, which supplies the substantive list and is therefore preferred for the definition quote. The process_role group fits because these courts are bodies in which proceedings under the Act may be brought. The Manual passages describe deferment practice associated with court proceedings; they do not define the statutory class. Other cited provisions are not supplied in full, so their precise contribution cannot be confirmed from these passages."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s190> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check the currency of the supplied section 190 court list before using it as a statement of current law."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0139" ;
    tmk:hearsAppealsFrom tmkc:GC-0133 ;
    tmk:labelKey "prescribed court" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s190>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6> ;
    tmk:notLabel "Administrative Review Tribunal (ART)"@en-AU,
