tmkc:GC-0144 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A subpoena is a court-issued document requiring a named person to attend court to give oral evidence, produce documents or other things, or both."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "subpoena"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly defines a subpoena as a court-issued document and describes its service on, and handling by, the Registrar of Trade Marks. It is a distinct procedural instrument, not a goods or services category, generic phrase or existing concept. The Manual passages describe practice and court requirements; they do not establish that the cited Trade Marks Act provisions ground the concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part54/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check the relevance of TMA1995/s154 and TMA1995/s202(b): their text is not supplied, so their relationship to subpoenas cannot be verified from these passages."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0144" ;
    tmk:isServedOn tmkc:GC-0046,
        tmkc:GC-0159 ;
    tmk:labelKey "subpoena" ;
    tmk:notLabel "service of a subpoena"@en-AU,
        "subpoena for production"@en-AU,
        "subpoena to give evidence"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "service of a subpoena",
        "subpoena for production",
        "subpoena to give evidence" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "subpoena" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part54/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0144 .

tmkc:GC-0149 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "The holder's \"home\" Office under the Madrid system — the IP office of the Contracting Party the holder belongs to, through which requests may be presented to the International Bureau; where it is the Trade Marks Office, the Registrar performs its functions (reg 17A.10(3)). Relabelled on 2026-10-09 (ADR-0131) from \"Contracting Party of the holder\", which excluded its own Office — the only thing the Manual and the Regulations speak of."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Office of the Contracting Party of the holder"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S029" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "As first written the concept was the Contracting Party itself and listed \"Office of the Contracting Party of the holder\" as a label it must not be confused with; every passage that uses the term speaks of that Office, so recognition never found the concept and it connected to nothing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/contracting-party-of-the-holder> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the concept as now labelled is what the corpus uses."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0149" ;
    tmk:labelKey "office of the contracting party of the holder" ;
    tmk:notLabel "Madrid Protocol"@en-AU,
        "designated Contracting Parties"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "designated contracting party",
        "madrid protocol" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "office of the contracting party of the holder" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.10(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/contracting-party-of-the-holder> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0149 .

tmkc:GC-0152 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: This statutory expression identifies services attributable to a person through that person's dealing with or providing them in the course of trade."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "services of a person"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly defines the expression by reference to a person's trade activities. It is therefore a legal attribution concept, not merely a services category or generic phrase, and no existing concept duplicates it. The historical section 41 extracts illustrate its role in distinguishing an applicant's services from those of other persons. Subject_matter fits best because the expression identifies the services to which trade mark protection relates. Sections 8 and 7(3) are mentioned in nearby notes about authorised use, but the supplied passages do not establish them as grounds for this definition."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.4e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/services-of-a-person> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check whether subject_matter is the preferred grouping for statutory attribution concepts; the supplied section 41 extracts concern the version prior to Raising the Bar, not necessarily the current provision."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0152" ;
    tmk:labelKey "service of a person" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised use"@en-AU,
        "classification of goods and services"@en-AU,
        "specification of goods and services"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "authorised use",
        "classification of good and service",
        "specification of good and service" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "service of a person" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/services-of-a-person> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0152 .

tmkc:GC-0157 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:Context,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A Convention country is a prescribed foreign country or region whose status is relevant to claiming priority from an earlier trade mark application filed there."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "convention country"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Convention country"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly defines a legally significant category of foreign country or region. The Manual explains its relevance to priority under section 29 and describes the prescriptions in regulation 21.29. It is distinct from the existing convention application concept: it identifies the qualifying jurisdiction, not the application. relevant_factor fits best because this status feeds into priority entitlement; the country or region is not itself a treaty or an actor in the described process."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/convention-country> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check regulation 21.29 directly for the prescribed countries and regions, as its content is supplied only through the Manual extract; also confirm the relevant_factor grouping."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0157" ;
    tmk:labelKey "convention country" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s29>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r21.29> ;
    tmk:notLabel "Paris Convention"@en-AU,
        "convention application"@en-AU,
        "priority date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "convention application",
        "paris convention",
        "priority date" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "convention country" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/convention-country> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0157 .

