tmkc:GC-0135 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: Cessation of protection is the ending of protection for a protected international trade mark, with the Manual describing procedures for seeking cessation for non-use."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "cessation of protection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define the term, and the Manual describes applications and opposition procedures concerning cessation for non-use. It names an event ending protection and therefore fits procedural_step. It is distinct from removal for non-use of a registered trade mark: the supplied definition concerns a protected international trade mark. No existing concept expressly covers this event. The listed legislative provisions cannot be assessed as grounding provisions without their text."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.48/cessation-of-protection> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Confirm the scope of the definition in regulation 17A.48 and which of the listed provisions provide its legislative basis; their substantive text was not supplied."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0135" ;
    tmk:labelKey "cessation of protection" ;
    tmk:notLabel "extension of protection"@en-AU,
        "removal for non-use"@en-AU,
        "revocation of registration"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "extension of protection",
        "removal for non use",
        "revocation of registration" ;
    tmk:operatesOn tmkc:GC-0114 ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "cessation of protection" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.48/cessation-of-protection> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0135 .

tmkc:GC-0143 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: Extension of protection is the extension to Australia of protection for the trade mark that is the subject of an IRDA."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "extension of protection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define the term, making it a distinct legal concept rather than a generic phrase. The Manual explains that an IRDA requests extension of protection in Australia and is not an application for registration. The extension is distinct from the IRDA that requests it (GC-0113) and the protected international trade mark status (GC-0114). Procedural_step is the closest fit for the event extending protection to Australia."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.29/extension-of-protection> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Confirm whether procedural_step best captures the extension itself, rather than the request for extension or the resulting protected status."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0143" ;
    tmk:isCommencedBy tmkc:GC-0113 ;
    tmk:labelKey "extension of protection" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.29> ;
    tmk:notLabel "application for registration"@en-AU,
        "extension of time"@en-AU,
        "international registration designating Australia"@en-AU,
        "protected international trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "application for registration",
        "extension of time",
        "international registration designating australia",
        "protected international trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "extension of protection" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.29/extension-of-protection> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0143 .

tmkc:GC-0160 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A registration number is the identifying number the Registrar must give a trade mark on registration, which the Manual lists among the particulars entered in the Register."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "registration number"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly defines the term by reference to subsection 68(2), which requires the Registrar to allocate an identifying number on registration. It is a specific statutory identifier, not a generic phrase or a duplicate of the registered trade mark or Register concepts. The Manual separately describes its recording in the Register and its use in consent letters and defensive applications. Instrument_or_record is the closest group because the number is a recorded registration particular, although it is not itself a document."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s68(2)> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check whether the ontology treats an identifying number recorded in the Register as an instrument_or_record or as a data attribute."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0160" ;
    tmk:isPartOf tmkc:GC-0150 ;
    tmk:isRecordedIn tmkc:GC-0161,
        tmkc:GC-0165 ;
    tmk:labelKey "registration number" ;
    tmk:notLabel "Register of Trade Marks"@en-AU,
        "application number"@en-AU,
        "registered trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "application number",
        "register of trade mark",
        "registered trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "registration number" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s68(2)> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0160 .

