tmkc:GC-0133 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: Commission is the statutory shorthand for the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission, a body with procedural functions identified in the supplied Manual passages."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "ACCC"@en-AU,
        "Australian Competition and Consumer Commission"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Commission"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 expressly identifies a specific statutory body, distinct from the existing concepts, so the term warrants a process_role concept. The Manual passages identify that body in connection with time allowances and matters sent to it during deferment; these are statements of practice, not legislative definitions. The generic lower-case use of 'commission' in the ownership passage does not identify this defined body. Only section 6 is supplied as legislative text, so the other cited provisions cannot be verified as legislative grounds for its functions here."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/commission> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check the precise functions under the cited Part 16 provisions and regulations, whose text has not been supplied."@en-AU ;
