    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0127 .

tmkc:GC-0131 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A trade mark application is an application seeking registration of a trade mark under section 27, including a representation of the mark and a specification of the relevant goods and/or services."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "application for registration of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "trade mark application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define the term, and section 27 supplies the application requirements and required contents. The application is best treated as an instrument or record, rather than the act of filing or the trade mark sought to be registered. No existing concept covers the general application: divisional and convention applications are more specific concepts, while examination, acceptance and amendment concern its processing. The regulatory definition is substantive rather than merely a direction to another definition, so it is retained as the definition quote."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2/trade-mark-application> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check whether the definition in regulation 5.2 has a limited contextual scope before adopting it throughout the ontology."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0131" ;
    tmk:labelKey "application for registration of a trade mark",
        "trade mark application" ;
    tmk:notLabel "amendment of an application"@en-AU,
        "convention application"@en-AU,
        "divisional application"@en-AU,
        "examination"@en-AU,
        "trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "amendment of an application",
        "convention application",
        "divisional application",
        "examination",
        "trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "trade mark application" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2/trade-mark-application> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0131 .

tmkc:GC-0159 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A Deputy Registrar is a distinct trade marks office-holder whom the Manual identifies as acting in acceptance, proposed revocation notification and the direction of Register rectification."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "Deputy Registrar of Trade Marks"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Deputy Registrar"@en-AU ;
    tmk:actsUnderDirectionOf tmkc:GC-0046 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S026" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-08"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Legislative basis corrected (review F3): Section 203 is the Registrar's duty to give a person a hearing before exercising a power adversely; the office of Deputy Registrar is section 205, which the record already cites."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/deputy-registrar> ;
    tmk:exercisesPowersOf tmkc:GC-0046 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check the appointment and powers provisions, particularly sections 203 and 205, whose text was not supplied, before adding a fuller statutory description of the office."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0159" ;
    tmk:issues tmkc:GC-0127 ;
    tmk:labelKey "deputy registrar",
        "deputy registrar of trade mark" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s205> ;
    tmk:notLabel "Examination team leader"@en-AU,
        "Registrar"@en-AU,
        "Registrar of Trade Marks"@en-AU,
        "acceptance officers"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "acceptance officer",
        "examination team leader",
        "registrar",
        "registrar of trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:performs tmkc:GC-0040,
        tmkc:GC-0042,
        tmkc:GC-0128 ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "deputy registrar" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/deputy-registrar> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0159 .

tmkc:GC-0161 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: The International Register is the register maintained by the International Bureau for the purposes of the Madrid Protocol, in which international registrations and subsequent designations are recorded."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "International Register"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define a specific register, making this a legal record rather than a generic phrase. Regulation 2.1 points to regulation 17A.2, so the substantive definition is preferred. The Manual describes international registrations and subsequent designations being recorded in it. It is distinct from the existing concepts for the Register of Trade Marks, the International Bureau, the Madrid Protocol and international registration of a trade mark."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/international-register> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check any additional legislative links to the listed cited provisions, whose text was not supplied."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0161" ;
    tmk:labelKey "international register" ;
    tmk:notLabel "International Bureau"@en-AU,
        "Madrid Protocol"@en-AU,
        "Record of International Registrations"@en-AU,
        "Register of Trade Marks"@en-AU,
        "international registration of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "international bureau",
        "international registration of a trade mark",
        "madrid protocol",
        "record of international registration",
        "register of trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "international register" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/international-register> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0161 .

tmkc:GC-0162 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: Change of ownership encompasses assignment or transmission of a trade mark from one party to another, rather than a name change by the same entity."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "change in ownership"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "change of ownership"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly identify change of ownership as including assignment or transmission. It is a useful umbrella concept rather than a duplicate of GC-0086 assignment or GC-0087 transmission individually. The Manual explains the passing of ownership between parties, distinguishes it from a change of name by the same entity, and describes recordal under section 110. The ownership-transfer event fits procedural_step; the Manual's account of recordal is practice guidance, not itself legislation."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.4e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/change-of-ownership> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check the scope of the regulation 17A.2 definition, which appears in the international-registration context, before applying it as a statutory definition across all trade marks."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0162" ;
    tmk:labelKey "change in ownership",
        "change of ownership" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s110> ;
    tmk:notLabel "change of name"@en-AU,
        "recordal of change of ownership"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "change of name",
        "recordal of change of ownership" ;
    tmk:operatesOn tmkc:GC-0113,
        tmkc:GC-0114 ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "change of ownership" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/change-of-ownership> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0162 .

